COMMENT ON TABLE public.ad_metrics IS 'One row per tracker row with the family''s since-launch and trailing-window metrics, carried by the FIRST row of the family (others read 0). Behind the Tags tables of the app. Grain: one row per tracker_row_id. Source: etl.build_metrics from meta_ad_lifetime + family_daily + meta_family_map + meta_ads (Meta-reported). Refresh: nightly: TRUNCATE and rebuild. Coverage: 3,980 rows, 3,889 first rows. Caveats: Metrics sit on the first row of each family_key across ALL products (the tracker row whose product matches the family name, else a real product over ''unassigned'', else the lowest sheet_row); the other rows read 0. Rows with a blank ad family (''id:...'') always read 0 because their spend cannot be matched. | Since launch = Meta all-time lifetime per ad summed over the family''s Meta ads: no cutoff rule and no launch-date gate. The *_7d / *_30d columns end on the last complete day. | The *_active columns are the same figures over currently ACTIVE ads only.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.tracker_row_id IS 'tracker_rows.id (primary key).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.product_id IS 'products.id.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.family_key IS 'Tracker family key.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.is_first_row IS 'true on the row that carries the family''s metrics.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.launch_date IS 'Launch date of the row (tracker).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.spend_launch IS 'Since-launch spend, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.purchases_launch IS 'Since-launch Meta-reported purchases (rounded to whole numbers).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.revenue_launch IS 'Since-launch Meta-reported purchase value, dollars.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.spend_7d IS 'Spend over the 7 days ending the last complete day.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.purchases_7d IS 'Purchases over those 7 days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.revenue_7d IS 'Purchase value over those 7 days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.spend_30d IS 'Spend over the 30 days ending the last complete day.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.purchases_30d IS 'Purchases over those 30 days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.revenue_30d IS 'Purchase value over those 30 days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.live IS 'true when the family spent on either of the last two days.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN public.ad_metrics.built_at IS 'When the table was built.';
